      "powerDrawWatts": 4.1,
      "notes": "Granular effects and looper pedal. The stereo input is a single TRS jack carrying left on the tip and right on the ring, so a stereo source needs a TRS-to-dual-mono lead into it, while the outputs are two ordinary TS jacks. Full-size 5-pin DIN MIDI in and out/thru, and a 1/4\" expression input. Needs 9 V DC at more than 450 mA on a centre-negative barrel, which is the usual pedal polarity but the opposite of an Eventide H90 on the same board, and more current than a small daisy-chain supply will give it. Hologram do not publish a weight, and the firmware-update USB port is not documented, so neither is modelled. I/O taken from the Sound on Sound review rather than a published connector list.",
